---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
---

<Layout title="Terms and Conditions">
  <Header lang="en" client:load />
  
  <main class="flex-grow bg-brand-bg pt-12 pb-16">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 md:px-12 bg-white p-8 md:p-12 shadow-sm rounded-lg">
      <h1 class="font-cinzel text-2xl md:text-3xl text-brand-text font-bold mb-8 text-center uppercase tracking-wider">Terms and Conditions</h1>
      
      <div class="space-y-6 text-brand-text/80 leading-relaxed text-xs md:text-sm">
        <section>
          <p class="mb-3">Welcome to Hotel Plaza San Antonio. The following terms and conditions govern your use of our website and booking of accommodation services. By making a reservation or utilizing our portal, you formally accept these terms in full.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-bold text-xl text-brand-text mb-3">1. Reservations and Payments</h2>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-3 space-y-2">
            <li>All reservation requests remain subject to room availability and formal written confirmation from hotel management.</li>
            <li>Guaranteeing reservations may necessitate valid debit/credit card pre-authorization details or an upfront bank transfer deposit, depending upon rate tariff restrictions.</li>
            <li>Published room prices reflect applicable national sales taxes unless clearly indicated otherwise (non-resident foreign tourists visiting Peru may qualify for exemption from the 18% IGV VAT upon presenting valid passports and Andean Migration Cards at check-in).</li>
            <li>Outstanding accommodation balances must be settled upon check-in or checkout according to reception procedures and booked tariff conditions.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-bold text-xl text-brand-text mb-3">2. Check-in and Check-out Policies</h2>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-3 space-y-2">
            <li><strong>Check-in (Arrival):</strong> From 1:00 PM (13:00) onwards (subject to room readiness; please notify reception of early arrivals).</li>
            <li><strong>Check-out (Departure):</strong> Until 12:00 PM (Noon).</li>
            <li>Requests regarding early arrivals (early check-in) or delayed departure times (late check-out) strictly rely on hotel room occupancy and may trigger supplementary hourly charges.</li>
            <li>At check-in, every registering guest must display an official physical identity document (National ID DNI, valid international passport, or foreign alien resident card).</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-bold text-xl text-brand-text mb-3">3. Cancellation and Modification Policies</h2>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-3 space-y-2">
            <li>Specific reservation cancellation terms rely directly upon the promotional rate category selected during online booking; please inspect tariff conditions before confirming reservations.</li>
            <li>Standard flexible tariffs require formal notice submitted prior to designated booking cutoff windows to prevent monetary penalties (customarily equivalent to a one-night accommodation charge).</li>
            <li>In circumstances of "No Show" (failure to arrive on confirmed arrival dates without advance notification), the hotel will bill the initial overnight stay or total reservation balance in line with selected booking constraints.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-bold text-xl text-brand-text mb-3">4. Hotel Rules and Regulations</h2>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-3 space-y-2">
            <li><strong>Smoking Policy:</strong> Smoking is strictly forbidden within bedrooms, interior hallways, breakfast rooms, and all covered common property areas. Special deep-cleaning fees will apply should guests violate interior smoke prohibitions.</li>
            <li><strong>Pet Policy:</strong> Please communicate with reception prior to booking regarding companion animal allowances, as pets may be restricted or subject to distinct accommodation conditions and sanitation surcharges.</li>
            <li><strong>Property Damage:</strong> Registered guests retain financial responsibility regarding accidental or intentional harm caused to hotel fixtures, equipment, structural finishes, or linens during their residency; management reserves the right to charge appropriate repair or full item replacement costs.</li>
            <li><strong>Guest Conduct:</strong> Visitors are expected to demonstrate civil, courteous, and respectful manners towards fellow patrons and hotel hospitality personnel; management retains statutory rights of admission and order enforcement.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-bold text-xl text-brand-text mb-3">5. Property Liability</h2>
          <p class="mb-3">Hotel Plaza San Antonio EIRL cannot assume legal liability concerning damage, loss, or theft of unprotected money, jewelry, electronic hardware, or travel credentials left unsecured inside guest chambers. We strongly urge guests to utilize personal room security boxes.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-bold text-xl text-brand-text mb-3">6. Policy Modifications</h2>
          <p class="mb-3">Hotel Plaza San Antonio reserves the right to revise or adjust these Terms and Conditions at management's discretion. Updated regulatory clauses come into legal effect immediately following publication on this official domain.</p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
  
  <Footer lang="en" />
</Layout>
